---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Dan Betts — The Breaking Dad"
  description="Dan Betts is a UK dad based in Hampshire. Eight years into co-parenting his daughter Evie, six years into blended family life. He writes about separated parenting, family life, and the products he actually uses."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <div class="container--narrow">

      <nav class="about-page__breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
        <span aria-current="page">About</span>
      </nav>

      <div class="about-page__photo-header">
        <img
          src="/images/dan-betts.jpg"
          alt="Dan Betts — The Breaking Dad"
          width="120"
          height="120"
          loading="eager"
          class="about-page__photo"
        />
        <div>
          <h1 class="about-page__name">Dan Betts</h1>
          <p class="about-page__location">Hampshire, UK</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">

        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
          I'm Dan. Dad to three daughters, step-dad to two more. I separated from Evie's mum in
          2016 when Evie was two years old. Since then I've been co-parenting her on a shared
          arrangement — eight years and counting — while also navigating the complexities of
          blended family life with my partner Rosie, her two daughters, and our youngest, Millie.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started The Breaking Dad because I couldn't find the writing I needed when
          I needed it most. Everything I found about separated parenting was either clinical,
          legal, or soaked in judgment. None of it sounded like a real person. None of it
          acknowledged how hard the early days actually are, or how messy the emotions get
          even when you're trying your best.
        </p>

        <h2>Why I write what I write</h2>
        <p>
          The Separated parents section is built from experience. I've navigated the CMS.
          I've been through mediation. I've introduced Rosie to Evie — not overnight, and not
          without anxiety. I've had to learn about child arrangements, benefits, and the
          financial side of separation the hard way. I write about what I've actually lived,
          and I signpost to proper resources when something is genuinely outside my lane.
        </p>
        <p>
          The reviews are honest in the old-fashioned sense — I buy things, I use them for
          months or years, and then I write about whether they were worth it. I've got affiliate
          links on some of them, but I don't let that change what I say.
          <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Full disclosure here</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Diary section is where I write without a brief. No SEO targets, no keyword
          strategy. Just personal pieces about what it actually feels like to be a dad in the
          middle of all this.
        </p>

        <h2>The family</h2>
        <p>
          Rosie and I have been together since 2018 and moved in together in 2020 — which,
          in retrospect, was either brave or slightly mad, given that we did it in a pandemic
          with three girls under ten. Millie, our youngest, arrived in 2021. So we went from
          zero to a household of six fairly quickly.
        </p>
        <p>
          Evie is twelve now. She's funny and fierce and reads more books than anyone I know.
          Rosie's girls are at secondary school. Millie has just started school and is absolutely
          convinced she runs the house. She might be right.
        </p>
        <p>
          We live in Hampshire. I work from home. I drink a lot of strong tea. I run in
          Vivobarefoot shoes. I am occasionally found building cardboard structures with small
          children on weekend afternoons.
        </p>

        <h2>Work with me</h2>
        <p>
          If you're a brand that wants to work with me, please read the
          <a href="/work-with-us/">Work with us</a> page first. I only work with brands
          whose products I'd genuinely consider using myself, and I don't take payments to
          change my editorial position.
        </p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          The best way to reach me is via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
          I do read everything, though I can't always reply as quickly as I'd like.
        </p>

        <p>
          You can also find me on Instagram:
          <a href="https://www.instagram.com/thebreakingdad" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            @thebreakingdad
          </a>.
          I'm most active there and usually respond to DMs faster than email.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    padding-block: 2rem 5rem;
  }

  .about-page__breadcrumb {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .about-page__breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .about-page__breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .about-page__photo-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about-page__photo {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 3px solid var(--color-highlight);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .about-page__name {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
  }

  .about-page__location {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
